  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Angolensin may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Angolensin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4A, which is then targeted by (10R)-10-[(E)-2-[(2S,3S)-3-[(Z)-pent-2-enyl]oxiran-2-yl]ethenyl]oxecan-2-one, a compound that ultimately targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The second pathway connects Angolensin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4A, which is also targeted by deferoxamine, another compound that ultimately targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The third pathway links Angolensin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4A, which is targeted by 4-Formylaminooxyvinylglycine, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively suggest that Angolensin may modulate Phosphodiesterase 6C through the regulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4A, which acts as a central mediator in these interactions. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a potential mechanism involving the regulation of demethylase activity, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated."
